Old Labour:-

Key labour principles embodying nationalisation, redistribution of wealth from rich to poor and the provision of continually improving welfare and state services, which largely rejected Thatcherite / free-market reforms or a Blairite approach.

New Labour:-

A revision of the traditional labour values and ideals represented by Old Labour. Influenced by Anthony Giddens, the 'Third Way' saw Labour shift in emphasis from a heavy focus on a working class to a wider class base, and a less robust alliance with the trade unions.
